{{\textless}p{\textgreater}Reminds} me again: http://www.culturechange.org/sail\_transport\_network.html{\textless}/p{\textgreater}
{{\textless}p{\textgreater}We} can't really predict what innovations in transport will occur. I need to work much more on this notion of what we can and cannot know about the {future.The} changes {CAT} claim can be expected look more like a list of desired land use changes; if that's true, they need to argue this, and distinguish the two. The transition movement make this mistake: conflating their expectations and their predictions.{\textless}/p{\textgreater}
