{{\textless}li{\textgreater}UK} agri - 3.3 {TWh} per annum, which I get to be 0.00376 terawatts, i.e about 1.2\% of total {UK} energy consumption. {\textless}/li{\textgreater}
{\textless}li{\textgreater}54\% of that attributable to nitrogen production, apparently. {\textless}/li{\textgreater}
{{\textless}li{\textgreater}Notes} - Haber bosch process = 1.3\% of world fossil fuel consumption, but that some {GWP} analyses show industrial ammonia can reduce overall co2 through efficiency gains - more output per hectare, lower relative co2.{\textless}em{\textgreater} {[Cranfield} University Institute of Water and Environment: {EnvironmentalBurdens} of Agricultural and Horticultural Commodity Production, Defra-funded Projects {IS0205} and {IS0222]{\textless}/em{\textgreater}{\textless}/li{\textgreater}}
