},

@misc{geyrhalter_our_2005,
	title = {Our Daily Bread},
	author = {Nikolaus Geyrhalter},
	year = {2005},
	annote = {{{\textless}p{\textgreater}Our} daily bread notes{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br {/{\textgreater}Alien} green tommyknocker light, machine sprays{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}cows in a bizarre merrygoround{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}vast co0rridors stacks baby chicks 10{\textless}br /{\textgreater}being shot out of the machine a blur{\textless}br /{\textgreater}lady processes, click, unexplained purpose – she's fast. All the menial jobs – women. {\textless}br {/{\textgreater}Time} motion study, looks like{\textless}br /{\textgreater}some human touches – barn workers eats sandwiches for lunch (just to remind us we've been looking at food.){\textless}br /{\textgreater}potatoes coming up from a vast field on a giant converyor taking them from the soil; hard to imagine anything human ever achieving this.{\textless}br /{\textgreater}men don gasmasks, overalls, gloves – presumably dealing with some naasty chems, under plastic – huge greenhouse{\textless}br /{\textgreater}spraying peppers, dense fine mist{\textless}br {/{\textgreater}Now} stripping to waist another picks same by hand – choosing ripe ones{\textless}br {/{\textgreater}Woman} doing same with tomatoes – claustrophobic, no other sounds but her cutting tomatoes from the vine{\textless}br {/{\textgreater}sHE} stops to have a cigarette{\textless}br /{\textgreater}long shot of greenhouses at night – acres, orange light{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}massive bulls, semen testing; men have to intervene in staged coitus, {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}such an array of machinery: tractor built to fill bull pens with hay; they're in there, getting covered in the stuff: huge energy use; {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}calf born by caesarian, mother still stands, huge wound{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}tractor unfolds its wings with high-pitched squeal; {\textless}br /{\textgreater}/ {\textless}br /{\textgreater}generally show spraying followed by picking – eidtorial choice; then lanes full of apples in water, robots working overhead – still people packing though.{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}finally arranged presentably – turned by hand, packs of six. Pneumatic sounds of machinery. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}workers bused in to farm- long drive, old bus; they plant, checked by a supervisor with binoculors{\textless}br /{\textgreater}irrigated at the end of the day{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}pigs off lorry; into narrow tube, squeeling – not entirely clear what happens next, but they come out dead or unconscious, and are hung up by another man. one man cuts tendons. entirely automatically gutted; embraced closely by the machine as they're cut. once cut open its a human job, the conveyor moving at a set speed.{\textless}br /{\textgreater}one woman's job, sitting, powered claw to slice off trotters; another to separate innards onto two conveyors by hand; christ knows where each part is going{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}and there's the canteen; the contrast, of  course, is the thing. Stuffing food in quickly from plastic containers,l though one lady does have home made samichs / eating with industrial noise still in background{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}from pig to beautiful sunflower field – phew! sprayed by biplane. I think perhaps that killed them; they're then harvested by a clawed tractor. black carcases. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}night harvested lettuce; exactly the opposite, entirely slow. Row of workers on knees slice and put in trays; tractor drives a foot at a time – is there a driver?{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br {/{\textgreater}Oh} – the merrygoround is a milking device. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}cucumbers in again vast greenhouses, looks like spain, harvested by prob migrant workers. For lunch they share a huge bowl of rice, watch telly in a run-down common room, paint peeling off wall. Others share some lunch in the sun on an olive farm. a transformers-like tentacle grips trees base, vibrates it for thirty seconds; floor is then hoovered by another machine. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}olive grove stretching over many hills{\textless}br /{\textgreater}/{\textless}br /{\textgreater}men deep underground; shaft must be a mile at least; they then drive underground... what can this possibly have to do with food? Oh – is it a potassium mine? Oh my god the diggers are vast machines. theyre blowing a channel, scooping the rock away with these huge diggers. walls like cliffs. just seems to be two of them working down there. out it comes in powder liquid form. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br {/{\textgreater}I'm} struck by the arbitrary things machines can't do / its cheaper to use people for: lining salmon up a person's job; a machine does all the slicing and gutting with a few mechanical arms at great speed{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}the pigs on their side in pens, utterly unable to move, with piglets on the other side of the metal feeding, great rows, filmed from above. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}squeel of piglets being de-tailed (they chew them off) is unbelievable.  Cleaning – high pressure hoses everywhere, what would happen without these?{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}more chemicals at the end of the process{\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}yikes – chicken hoover. lifts them from the barn floor, they're packed in there. so it can just sweep back and forth. stuffed into crates, doors slammed. well – machine dispenses them at high speed. specially designed hoover – someone's really thought about that. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}fordism, entirely. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}cows – blood comes out from the heart, cut into. {\textless}br /{\textgreater}{\textless}br /{\textgreater}cleaning chicken factory – every available surface. Place designed that way I guess.{\textless}/p{\textgreater}}
},

