{{\textless}li{\textgreater}They} can also consult a small number of other agents [6 I think], who can report the utility they got from whichever they chose. Clearly, this random sampling will better indicate the true spread (within a given probability.){\textless}/li{\textgreater}
{{\textless}li{\textgreater}Agents} have 'rules of thumb' for choosing; experience can change the rules of thumb. [heuristics]{\textless}/li{\textgreater}
